# Canada — Lists
# answer-mode: type
# answer-case: insensitive

Name the three territories
---
+ Yukon
= The Yukon
+ Northwest Territories
= NWT
+ Nunavut
---
North of 60. Nunavut is the newest, split from the Northwest Territories
in 1999.

Name the three Maritime provinces
---
+ New Brunswick
= NB
+ Nova Scotia
= NS
+ Prince Edward Island
= PEI
---
Newfoundland and Labrador is Atlantic Canada but not a Maritime province —
the Maritimes were named long before it joined Confederation in 1949.

Name the three Prairie provinces
---
+ Alberta
+ Saskatchewan
+ Manitoba
---
West to east. Only Saskatchewan is entirely prairie-flat cliché; Alberta
has the Rockies and Manitoba the Shield.

Name five of the ten provinces
---
quota: 5
+ British Columbia
= BC
+ Alberta
+ Saskatchewan
+ Manitoba
+ Ontario
+ Quebec
+ New Brunswick
+ Nova Scotia
+ Prince Edward Island
= PEI
+ Newfoundland and Labrador
= Newfoundland
---
Ten provinces and three territories. The four originals of 1867: Ontario,
Quebec, New Brunswick, Nova Scotia.
